      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLAT OUT FREDDY (1) is a talented type and proved too classy last time to win by 1.1 lengths at this track in a handy 30.40 beating Stomper Romper. The hardest to beat again. WHITE MOCHA (7) is a strong stayer who excels over the longer races. Was a winner last time (29.53) over 515m at Sandown in a Grade 5 and is even better suited at the extra journey. Goes very well at the journey winning two races. Expecting another bold showing. LAKEVIEW LEIGH (6) drew a squeeze box and was game in defeat when a close second, a nose from the winner Little Lockett (34.61) at this track. Consistent performer from this draw with a win and two minor placings to her credit. Overdue and expected to feature again. MOONLIGHT MILLER (3) has ability and finds the right scenario to bounce back.",
